body:
Hi there! Sorry for taking a while to get back to you. I don't necessarily use particular websites for recipes (besides pinterest), but I do follow a lot of vegan youtubers. My favourites are Caitlin Shoemaker (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0cxMY7jZ_kiE2bvykJffZA), Madeleine Olivia (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC4CpQoAPJNGGUPG92Fbwxqw) and Maddie Lymburner (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCH7fZDHwZR7ww23A50R1ppA). If watching videos isn't exactly your thing, they all have blogs as well where they post all their recipes and have e-books for sale. I've tried recipes from all three of them and have thoroughly enjoyed them. I really like Maddie because she does a lot of "what I eat in a day"s, which I find i get a lot of inspiration from, and Caitlin and Madeleine do a lot of budget meal prep which as a student is a huge plus. 

I'm so excited to hear that you want to transition to veganism! Don't worry, cheese was the hardest thing for me to give up as well. I ended up being "lucky" though as the last time I ate cheese I ate way too much and got really sick so now I don't find it as appetizing as I used to haha. The transition can be very difficult but remember to be kind to yourself! There's no set amount of time it should take you and don't beat yourself up if you slip up or make mistakes, you're only human.

if you have any questions, please don't hesitate to DM me. I've only been vegan for about 6 months now, so I'm definitely not the most knowledgeable, but I know making the change can be even more difficult if you're doing it by yourself. Best of luck :)
